<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61227" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλακρέτ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, name of a financial official in early
		Athens and elsewhere (cf. foreg.), <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12.19.13
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>Ath.</u>
			7.3
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>V.</u>
			695
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Av.</u>
			1541
		</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλακρέτου γάλα</span>, comically
		for the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθὸς δικαστικός</span>, <i><span class="en">
			Id.
			<u>V.</u>
			724
		</span></i>. (Written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλαγρ</span>- in Cod. Rav. of <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Tim.
			<u>Lex.</u>
		</span></i>; derivation from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλᾶς ἀγρεῖν</span>
		or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγείρειν</span> perh. implied by
			Suid.<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κωλακρέτης</span>
			.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
